From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 19:14:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Check a listed remote file's existence from its listing

When read_blob() or read_text() needs neither the content nor the
metadata of a remote file, DirectFileReader::Scan() checked that the file
exists with FileExists(file.path). The bare path drops the metadata the
glob's listing put into the OpenFileInfo, so httpfs sent one HEAD request
per file: selecting only filename from a glob over 500 objects took 500
requests, while selecting last_modified as well took none, because that
branch opens the file from the OpenFileInfo. The check now calls
GetStatsIfExists() with the OpenFileInfo. Where the listing carries
last_modified, etag and file_size, httpfs answers from it without a
request; where a store omits any of them, httpfs still sends a HEAD, so
the check is never more expensive than before, but not always free. A
literal path that does not exist still yields no rows, and local files
are not checked, as before.

The error behaviour changes. FileExists() turned every error into false,
so the file was skipped; GetStatsIfExists() turns only a missing file
into no row, so a 403, a 5xx or a credentials error now raises, as it
already does when size or last_modified is selected.

Opening the file with FILE_FLAGS_NULL_IF_NOT_EXISTS under
CACHE_REMOTE_ONLY, as the metadata branch does, is not an option: the
caching wrapper dereferences the null handle and fails with an internal
error.

Carried here until upstream takes it; upstream issue to be filed by the
maintainer, see duckdb/duckdb-r#2977.

---
 src/duckdb/src/function/table/direct_file_reader.cpp | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/function/table/direct_file_reader.cpp b/src/duckdb/src/function/table/direct_file_reader.cpp
index c84fdc485e..2b7e801c9e 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/src/function/table/direct_file_reader.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/function/table/direct_file_reader.cpp
@@ -80,9 +80,9 @@ AsyncResult DirectFileReader::Scan(ClientContext &context, GlobalTableFunctionSt
 			return SourceResultType::FINISHED;
 		}
 	} else {
-		// At least verify that the file exist
-		// The globbing behavior in remote filesystems can lead to files being listed that do not actually exist
-		if (is_remote && !fs.FileExists(file.path)) {
+		// A remote path the glob returned without full listing metadata is checked for existence;
+		// a listing entry that carries it is taken from the listing, as the remote metadata branch does
+		if (is_remote && !fs.GetStatsIfExists(file)) {
 			done.store(true, std::memory_order_relaxed);
 			return SourceResultType::FINISHED;
 		}
